 on 0.7x volume, closed on the low - no selling pressure after climactic strength: background has changed (low significance: marginal bar); balance strength 64/100.","status":"spring confirmed","last_sign":{"name":"No supply","d":"2026-10-06","pol":1,"sig":0.48,"tier":"low","why":"no selling pressure after climactic strength: background has changed","ref":null},"key_bars":[{"name":"Buying climax","d":"2026-07-23","pol":-1,"sig":1.79,"tier":"high"},{"name":"No demand","d":"2026-08-06","pol":-1,"sig":0.72,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"No demand","d":"2026-08-07","pol":-1,"sig":0.72,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"No demand","d":"2026-08-17","pol":-1,"sig":0.78,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Effort to fall","d":"2026-09-22","pol":-1,"sig":0.96,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Selling climax","d":"2026-09-24","pol":1,"sig":2.73,"tier":"high"}],"asof":null},"scores":{"overall":25,"group":"SIC 371x (Transportation Equipment)","group_rank":24,"group_n":41,"sector_rank":167,"sector_n":257,"earn":31}},"biz":{"name":"OSHKOSH CORP","desc":"Oshkosh Corporation provides purpose-built vehicles and equipment worldwide. The company operates through three segments: Access, Vocational, and Transport segment. The Access segment designs and manufactures aerial work platform and telehandlers for use in construction, industrial, and maintenance applications; and towing and recovery equipment, which includes carriers, wreckers, and rotators, as well as provides financing and leasing solutions, including rental fleet loans, leases, and floor plan and retail financing. This segment also offers equipment installation and sale of chassis and service parts, as well as offers parts and accessories. The Transport segment engages in the manufacture and sale of heavy, medium, and light tactical wheeled vehicles and related services for defense; and hauling combat vehicles, missile systems, ammunition, fuel, and troops and cargos. The Vocational segment offers custom and commercial firefighting equipment, fire apparatus, and emergency vehicles, including pumpers, aerial platform, ladder and tiller trucks, and tankers; light, medium, and heavy-duty rescue vehicles; and wildland rough terrain response other emergency response vehicles. This segment also produces and sells aircraft rescue and firefighting vehicles; airport ground support equipment; baggage, airport facility and operations, and equipment-monitoring technology services; refuse and recycling collection vehicles and components; and IMT-branded field service vehicles and truck-mounted cranes, frontline communications-branded simulators, command vehicles and other communication vehicles, and front-discharge concrete mixer vehicles. The company sells its products through direct sales representatives, dealers, and distributors. The company was formerly known as Oshkosh Truck Corporation. Oshkosh Corporation was founded in 1915 and is headquartered in Oshkosh, Wisconsin.","desc_src":"Yahoo Finance profile via yfinance (third-party)","sic":"3711","sic_desc":"Motor Vehicles & Passenger Car Bodies","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Farm & Heavy Construction Machinery","mcap":8263865856,"mcap_src":"Yahoo Finance profile (third-party, cached)","hq":"OSHKOSH, WI","exchange":"XNYS","fy_end":"1231","cik":775158,"state_inc":"WI","massive_note":"Massive ticker details not fetched yet (5 calls/min limit; filled in on a nightly run)","sec_asof":"2026-10-09"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"Yahoo quarterly income statement via yfinance (third-party fallback)","asof":"2026-10-03","q":[{"end":"2025-06-30","rev":2732100000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":3.16,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":204800000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":7.5,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2025-09-30","rev":2688600000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":3.04,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":196200000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":7.3,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2025-12-31","rev":2688800000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":2.1,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":133800000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":5.0,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2026-03-31